Spec: LibBuildContext

Platform: Rhai script library (vynil-core 0.7.7 engine)

Purpose:
  Build the render/execution `context` map every instance operation and the offline
    template lane runs on: the shared assembly of `cluster` (agent.yaml + live or
    enum-default storage classes/CRDs/nodes/services), `controller`, `instance`
    (identity, package metadata, labels, selector, images, resources, appslug,
    current/requested tags), `values` masked from `defaults`, plus `defaults`,
    `package_dir` and `config_dir`. Two lanes of one contract: @template renders a
    cluster-free context from hardcoded profiles for offline `agent template`, and
    @run gathers the same shape from the real cluster for install/update flows. Since
    this is Rhai and not plain Rust, every failure mode is an interpreter error unless
    this file wraps it.

Exposes:
  @template(instance, args) — offline context builder, the `template` entry point name
    recognized by @ENTRY_POINT_FUNCTIONS (/agent/src/linting/rhai_checker.rs); reads no
    cluster object.
  @run(instance, args) — live context builder, the `run` entry point; the only lane that
    touches @k8s_resource and @get_tenant_name.
  @appslug(pkg, inst), @get_default(def), @get_values(options, defaults),
    @get_default_context(args) — module-visible helpers (Rhai module functions are all
    importable), also reached by templates only through the frozen output keys.
  Importer convention `import "build_context" as build` then `build::template` /
    `build::run` — frozen in the three per-kind wrappers (Depends on); those wrappers
    own the hook chain (`context_pre`/`context_post`/…) and the lane-specific keys
    `template_dir`, `agent_image`, `tenant`, `namespace` — this file mints none of them.

Accepts:
  @instance — a typed CR @Dynamic or deserialized map. @template reads only
    `metadata.name` and `metadata.namespace` (ungated: missing either is an interpreter
    error; `spec` is never read, so the synthesized template-lane instance needs none).
    @run additionally reads `spec["package"]` (bracket index), `spec.jukebox`,
    `spec.category`, `spec.options`, and optional `status.tag` (guarded); when
    @type_of(instance) == `TenantInstance` it calls @instance.get_tenant_name().
  @args — map with keys read verbatim, both lanes unless noted: `package_dir`
    (holds `package.yaml`), `config_dir` (holds optional `agent.yaml`),
    `controller_values` (a JSON `string` — a non-string value fails @json_decode and
    degrades, see Handles), `vynil_namespace`, `tag` (the requested version, surfaced
    as `instance.requested` ungated). @template only: `context_name`, matched against
    the literal `HA` string (the @Contexts enum serde spelling,
    /agent/src/template/mod.rs); every other value — including absent — selects the
    simple profile.
  No environment variables, no Secret reads: every input is an `args` key, one of two
    files under the args dirs, or a cluster read.

Returns:
  One map with top-level keys `cluster`, `controller`, `instance`, `values`,
    `defaults`, `package_dir`, `config_dir` (the last two echo the args values).
  `cluster`: the decoded `${args.config_dir}/agent.yaml` map or `#{}` when @is_file is
    false, then ALWAYS overwritten: `storage_classes` (enriched, below), `crds` (list of
    name strings), `services` (`[]`), `vynil_namespace` (args value); overwritten only
    when the merged map lacks the key: `prefered_storage` (@get_prefered_sc of the
    enriched classes) and `ha` (boolean).
  `instance`: `name`, `namespace`, `package`, `labels`, `selector`, `images`,
    `resources`, `current`, `requested`, `appslug`.
    `package` — @template: `name` (pkg metadata), `jukebox` literal `box`, `category`,
      `app_version`, `options`; @run adds `type` (pkg metadata `type`) and
      `backup_affinity`, with `jukebox` from `spec.jukebox` — the template lane mints
      neither `type` nor `backup_affinity` keys at all (Tasks).
    `labels` — six keys, `app.kubernetes.io/name`, `app.kubernetes.io/instance`,
      `app.kubernetes.io/managed-by` literal `vynil`,
      `vynil.solidite.fr/owner-namespace`, `vynil.solidite.fr/owner-category`,
      `vynil.solidite.fr/owner-type`. Name source: pkg `metadata.name` in @template,
      `instance.spec["package"]` in @run; owner-type: literal `system` in @template
      (all three kinds), `pkg.metadata["type"]` in @run (Tasks).
    `selector` — the same `app.kubernetes.io/name` + `app.kubernetes.io/instance` pair,
      same per-lane sources.
    `images` / `resources` — passed through from `pkg.images` / `pkg.resources`
      untouched (raw-map values in @template, typed maps in @run).
    `current` — `""` always in @template; `instance.status.tag` when `status` and `tag`
      both exist in @run, else `""`. `requested` — `args.tag`.
    `appslug` — @appslug(package-name, instance-name) (below).
  `values` / `defaults` — `defaults` is the @get_default(pkg.options) map; @template
    returns `values` from `get_values(#{}, defaults)` (a top-level copy of `defaults` —
    the synthesized instance cannot supply options), @run from
    `get_values(instance.spec.options, defaults)`.

Raises:
  This file never calls @throw. Interpreter errors escape wherever unguarded:
    `package.yaml`: @template does @file_read + @yaml_decode of `${package_dir}/package.yaml`
      (missing file / bad YAML raise), @run does the typed @read_package_yaml
      (/common/src/vynilpackage.sdd — validation and normalization run only on this
      lane, Tasks); bad `${config_dir}/agent.yaml` YAML raises (the @is_file gate tests
      existence, not parseability); `instance.metadata.*` and `args.tag`,
      `args.vynil_namespace`, `args.package_dir`, `args.config_dir` missing keys/props;
      a `pkg.options` map whose entry is not itself a map breaks the
      `def[k]["default"]` index in @get_default.
  @run cluster reads are unguarded except the @ServiceInstance block: the
    `StorageClass` @k8s_resource @list, and the two @list_meta reads of kinds
    `CustomResourceDefinition` / `Node`, abort @run on failure; the
    tenant @get_tenant_name is inside the guarded block so its @Err leg degrades
    instead (a Rust-side panic from client build would not be catchable —
    /common/src/context.sdd).
  Missing map keys answer `()` rather than raising: the locked rhai `1.25.1` engine
    leaves `fail_on_invalid_map_property` at its default (`false`), so
    `agent.yaml`-absent fields, absent SC annotations, and absent `status` fields walk
    the guards as `()`; out-of-range array indexing and registered-CR property misses
    are a different lane (raise).

Handles:
  `controller_values` absent, non-JSON, or non-string — `try`/`catch` around
    @json_decode; @type_of(e) `string` is @log_warn'd verbatim, any other error
    @json_encode'd; `controller` stays `#{}` and no message is raised.
  @ServiceInstance gather failure (list, tenant-name, or shape) — same @log_warn
    pattern; `cluster.services` keeps its pre-seeded `[]` (the assembled list is
    assigned only at the end of the guarded block).
  `agent.yaml` absent — base `#{}`; own `prefered_storage`/`ha` in `agent.yaml` are
    kept, every other overwritten key above is replaced even if `agent.yaml` set it.
  `context_name` — exact `"HA"` gives the hardcoded profile; case differs → simple.
  `StorageClass` defaulting — `is_default` is annotation
    `storageclass.kubernetes.io/is-default-class` == `true` only; an absent
    `annotations` map yields `false`.
  Tenant visibility — in @run each `svc.status.services` entry gains
    `instance` and `package` submaps (overwriting any pre-existing values), and
    flattens its `service` payload into the entry (`s += s.service` then
    @remove) where present. For a @TenantInstance caller: untagged entries and entries
    whose `tenant` equals @get_tenant_name() are kept (tag removed on match); foreign
    tags are dropped. For every other caller type: `tenant`-tagged entries are dropped
    entirely. Entries under a `status` that is not a map or `status.services` that is
    not an array are skipped silently.
  Absent `pkg.options` (`()` or non-map) — `defaults` and `values` are `#{}`, matching
    the linting claim frozen at /agent/src/linting/hbs_checker.sdd.

Must:
  @appslug(pkg, inst): return @inst when @pkg equals @inst (no length guard); else when
    `${inst}-${pkg}` exceeds 28 characters return it cut by @truncate to 28 (rhai `len`
    and `truncate` are both char-based on the locked build); else return
    `${inst}-${pkg}`. Both lanes pass (package-name, instance-name) in that order, so
    the slug is `<instance>-<package>`.
  @get_default(def): `#{}` unless @def is a map; then copy each top-level key from
    `def[k]["default"]` — shallow, one level, missing `default` copies as `()` — so
    `defaults` keys mirror `pkg.options` key-for-key.
  @get_values(options, defaults): `()` options → return @defaults whole; two maps →
    recurse keyed off the `defaults` map keys only (result top-level keys are exactly
    `defaults` keys; option-only keys are dropped at every level, values from options
    where present, defaults otherwise); any other shape → return @options. Invariant:
    `values` top-level keys ⊆ `pkg.options` top-level keys.
  @get_default_context(args): `HA` → `nodes` of the eight names `master01`, `master02`,
    `master03`, `worker01`, `worker02`, `worker03`, `worker04`, `worker05`, a 156-name
    `crds` snapshot
    over 34 api-groups (cert-manager/acme, cilium, rook-ceph, the kubevirt family incl.
    CDI/snapshot/clone/pool/export/migrations/instancetype, flux toolkit, cnpg,
    rabbitmq, grafana + monitoring.coreos.com, traefik, secretgenerator, redis,
    objectbucket/objectstorage, whereabouts, namecheap, kuberest/kacp/vynil
    solidite.fr) — the verbatim list is source-of-truth; `scs` `rook-cephfs`
    (`storage.cephfs.csi.ceph.com`, default), `rook-ceph-block`
    (`storage.rbd.csi.ceph.com`), `local-path` (`rancher.io/local-path`). Else:
    `nodes` `["single"]`, `crds` `[]`, `scs` default-priority `local-path` alone.
    `ha` on this lane is `nodes.len() > 1` on that literal list, not a node read.
  Feed @classes_enrich the three-field maps only: @template passes the static `scs`
    profile entries; @run maps listed StorageClass objects to
    `#{name, provisioner, is_default}` before enrichment (all other SC fields are
    dropped, the annotation check above). The enriched list — with `volumeMode`,
    `capabilities`, `accessModes`, `allAccessModes` and the extra Block clone for raw
    drivers, per ./storage_class_enrich.rhai — is what lands in
    `cluster.storage_classes` on both lanes; @get_prefered_sc consumes that same
    enriched list.
  @run live reads: `cluster.crds` from @k8s_resource @list_meta of kind
    `CustomResourceDefinition` items' `metadata.name`; `cluster.ha` (when agent.yaml
    omits it) from @k8s_resource @list_meta of kind `Node`, count > 1;
    `cluster.services` gathered from a cluster-wide @k8s_resource @list of kind
    `ServiceInstance` under the Handles visibility rules.
  Emit the context keys exactly as spelled in Returns — those names are the contract
    surface for the counterpart contracts listed in Depends on (rendered placeholders,
    selector lookups, lint allowlists), so a rename there must be a coordinated change
    of both specs.
  Run the two lanes' package.yaml loads differently but never let it change key names:
    typed load on @run, raw @yaml_decode on @template.
  Import-time surface: the module body executes exactly one
    `import "storage_class_enrich" as sce` resolution plus six `fn` declarations
    (@appslug, @get_default, @get_values, @get_default_context, @template, @run) — no
    top-level statements log, call the engine, or mutate state at import.

Depends on:
  ./storage_class_enrich.rhai — @sce.classes_enrich + @sce.get_prefered_sc, the module
    this file imports at line 2; its spec ./storage_class_enrich.sdd is being written by
    a sibling agent and is not yet readable.
  ./../system/context.rhai, ./../service/context.rhai, ./../tenant/context.rhai — the
    only importers (`import "build_context" as build`); they own hook chains and
    kind-specific keys. Indirect lanes: `import "context"` in
    /agent/scripts/packages/test.rhai, the embedded snippets of
    /agent/src/template/{system,service,tenant}.rs and
    /agent/src/{system,service,tenant}/install.rs.
  wynil-core `0.7.7` script surface (registrars behind /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd):
    @file_read, @is_file, @yaml_decode, @json_decode, @json_encode, @log_warn,
    @k8s_resource(...).@list/@list_meta.
  /common/src/vynilpackage.sdd — @read_package_yaml typed load on the @run lane.
  /common/src/instancetenant.sdd — @TenantInstance.get_tenant_name (cluster read on the
    @tenant services path).
  ./gen_package.rhai — generated `.hbs` are the largest structural consumers of the
    key freeze: `{{instance.appslug}}`, `{{instance.namespace}}` and @ctx_have_crd over
    `cluster.crds`; ./gen_package.sdd owns its side. /agent/src/linting/hbs_checker.sdd
    records the runtime-root allowlist (`cluster`,`controller`,`instance`,`values`,
    `defaults`,`package_dir`,`config_dir` — it believes EXISTENT-ONLY without validating
    content) and the `values`-empty-without-options rule this file produces.
    ./storage_class_selector.rhai reads `cluster.storage_classes` and
    `cluster.prefered_storage` key names. Each is a counterpart contract, not a
    dependency call edge: this module imports none of them.
  @rhai `1.25.1` locked semantics: tolerant map-miss → `()`, char-based string
    `len`/`truncate`.

Tasks:
  [ ] Map every Scenario to a mock-engine test on the
    ./../../tests/rhai_lib.rs harness (`make_lib_script_with_k8s` StorageClass/CRD/
    Node/ServiceInstance mocks): today NO test imports `build_context` — neither
    ./../../tests/rhai_lib.rs nor ./../../tests/rhai_build.rs (the latter covers
    `packages/build.rhai` only) — and its `build_context_mock`/`build_instance_mock`
    fixtures are `#[allow(dead_code)]`, pointing at a non-existent
    `./../scripts/config` dir.
  [ ] Cover @template end-to-end over the shipped `./../packages` shape (package.yaml +
    optional agent.yaml fixtures) asserting the frozen key set of Returns.
  [ ] Pin the @get_default non-map-entry raise and @appslug's `()` interpolation edge
    (missing `metadata.name` stringifies as text into the slug) before deciding whether
    guards belong here.
  [ ] Decide the fate of the dead `build_context_mock` fixture (wire it into tests or
    delete it) — currently a lint-visible `#[allow(dead_code)]`.
  [?] @appslug: the equal-name branch skips the 28-char guard a DNS-1123 label needs,
    and truncation can END on the joining `-` when the instance name is exactly 27
    chars (`<27-char instance name>-` shape) — no sanitize/trim exists. Decide whether
    the cap and a trailing-dash trim apply to every branch.
  [?] @run maps `is_default` from the GA annotation only — the
    `beta.storageclass.kubernetes.io/is-default-class` spelling is not checked even
    though the code tolerates annotations being absent. Decide whether the beta
    annotation join is intended.
  [?] @template hardcodes `owner-type` `system` and omits `package.type` /
    `package.backup_affinity`, so a service/tenant `agent template` render produces a
    system-flavoured instance block; @run derives both from the package. Decide whether
    the template lane follows package type (/agent/src/linting/hbs_checker.sdd's root
    drift names the same seam).
  [?] Label/selector source drift: `app.kubernetes.io/name` comes from the package
    metadata on @template but from `instance.spec["package"]` on @run — equal in
    practice, divergent on any rename. Decide the canonical source.
  [?] @get_values silently drops every option key absent from `pkg.options` defaults
    (user-set instance options with no declaration vanish from `values`);
    /agent/src/linting/hbs_checker.sdd freezes the matching `properties` three-way
    drift on the lint side. Decide whether undeclared options pass through.
  [?] The HA `crds` snapshot is a static 156-name copy that will drift from any live
    cluster's installed set (its @run twin reads CRDs live). Decide whether the profile
    is maintained by hand or generated from `agent crds`.
  [?] The @tenant gather lists ServiceInstances cluster-wide rather than in the
    tenant/`vynil_namespace` scope. Decide whether the cross-namespace sweep is the
    intended visibility.

Done when:
  Every Scenario has a mock-engine test, the key-spelling of Returns is cross-checked
    against ./gen_package.sdd and /agent/src/linting/hbs_checker.sdd, the drift `[?]`s
    are decided, and `specdd lint` is green.

Scenario: appslug concat, cap and equal-name passthrough
  Given @appslug("web","web") — slug equals instance
  Then the answer is `web` even if a longer equal pair would exceed 28 chars
  Given @appslug("kube-prometheus-stack","monitoring")
  Then the answer is `monitoring-kube-prometheus-sta` — joined `<instance>-<package>`
    then cut at 28 characters
  Given @appslug("box","web")
  Then the answer is `web-box` untouched

Scenario: context_name selects the offline profile, case-sensitively
  Given @template args with `context_name` `HA`
  Then `cluster.ha` is `true` (8-node list) and `cluster.crds` holds the 156-name
    snapshot, `cluster.storage_classes` the enriched 3-entry profile (the
    `rbd.csi.ceph.com` raw driver adds its Block clone)
  But given `context_name` `ha` or absent
  Then `cluster.ha` is `false`, `crds` is `[]` and `storage_classes` is the enriched
    single `local-path`

Scenario: agent.yaml merge polarity
  Given `${config_dir}/agent.yaml` containing `ha` `false`, `prefered_storage`
    `#{}`, and a `vynil_namespace` `other`
  When either @template or @run builds the context
  Then `ha` and `prefered_storage` are the agent.yaml values kept, while
    `vynil_namespace`, `storage_classes`, `crds` and `services` are the assembly's
    values — the `.keys()` membership guard alone decides the first two

Scenario: controller_values garbage degrades with a warning
  Given `controller_values` is the string `not-json`
  When either lane runs
  Then `controller` is `#{}` and @log_warn carries the parse error text
  And no error escapes

Scenario: tenant callers see untagged and own-tagged services
  Given a @TenantInstance whose @get_tenant_name answers `acme` and a @ServiceInstance
    status.services entry tagged `tenant: acme` with a `service` payload
  When @run gathers `cluster.services`
  Then the entry is kept, the `tenant` key removed, `service` flattened into it, and
    `instance`/`package` submaps attached to it
  But given a @SystemInstance caller and an entry tagged `tenant: acme`
  Then no such entry appears in `cluster.services`

Scenario: @ServiceInstance gather failure yields empty services, not a failed run
  Given @k8s_resource @list of kind `ServiceInstance` raises
  When @run continues past the guarded block
  Then `cluster.services` is `[]` and the error text was @log_warn'd

Scenario: current tracks the live status tag only on the run lane
  Given an instance with `status.tag` `1.4.0` and `args.tag` `2.0.0`
  Then @run returns `instance.current` `1.4.0` and `requested` `2.0.0`
  But @template on any instance returns `current` `""`

Scenario: values mask and empty-options fallback
  Given `defaults` `#{a: 1, b: 2}` and instance options `#{a: 9, x: 5}`
  Then @get_values answers `#{a: 9, b: 2}` — `x` dropped, `b` from defaults
  Given options `()`
  Then @get_values answers `defaults` whole
  Given a package.yaml without `options` on @template
  Then both `defaults` and `values` are `#{}`

Scenario: missing package.yaml aborts the build
  Given `package_dir` without `package.yaml`
  When @template (raw read) or @run (@read_package_yaml) runs
  Then the interpreter surfaces the read/validation error — neither lane catches it
